.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
*.pem
terraform.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example

# prod.tfvars is committed non-secret fleet/sizing config (reviewable in PRs).
# public-repo-hygiene.test.ts scans it, so account-specific identifiers stay
# out of it and out of the tree:
#   - secrets.tfvars — tokens + identifiers overlay for local apply.
#   - backend.hcl    — carries the account-ID state bucket; CI passes the same
#                      values inline from GitHub Variables (TF_STATE_*), local
#                      copies backend.hcl.example, so the live file is never
#                      committed.
# CI injects secrets/identifiers as TF_VAR_* (see release-all.yml); local
# applies use the overlay:
#
#   terraform apply -var-file=environments/prod/prod.tfvars \
#                   -var-file=environments/prod/secrets.tfvars
environments/*/secrets.tfvars
environments/*/backend.hcl
!environments/*/backend.hcl.example

# Leftover local overlays for non-prod envs (DEV Hub was decommissioned).
# Prod config is committed; do not resurrect a blob secret for it.
environments/dev/*.tfvars
!environments/dev/*.tfvars.example
environments/test/*.tfvars
!environments/test/*.tfvars.example
